{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>That the daughters of Canaan were evil in the eyes of Isaac his father.</b> He thought this was because they opposed his will, as it says: וַתִּהְיֶיןָ מוֹרַת רוּחַ (Genesis 26:35). He went to Ishmael, and by this he showed that Isaac could have protested when Esau married the Canaanite women, had he given it his attention — just as Rebekah now stirred him up regarding Jacob."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:08.218328066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}